{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Issachar is a strong-boned donkey.</b> חֲמוֹר — possessor of bones, bearing the yoke of Torah — like a strong donkey that they load with a heavy burden." "<b>Couching between the saddlebags.</b> Like a donkey that walks by day and by night and has no lodging in a house — and when he wants to rest, he lies down between the boundaries, at the town borders where he leads merchandise there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:06.872988520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}